  "id": "Compound::DB01216 - Gene::6715",
  "verbalization": "Finasteride exhibits a strong binding interaction with Srd5a2, which is involved in steroid dehydrogenase activities, including 3-oxo-5-alpha-steroid 4-dehydrogenase and cholestenone 5-alpha-reductase. These activities are closely related to the metabolism of steroid hormones, and Srd5a1 is a known participant in these pathways. The evidence suggests that Finasteride may influence Srd5a1 through its interaction with Srd5a2, potentially modulating steroid metabolism. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, mechanistically plausible relationship, with Srd5a2 acting as a bridge between Finasteride and Srd5a1. The shared involvement of Srd5a1 in steroid dehydrogenase activities implies that Finasteride could exert a biological effect through this pathway, possibly by altering the activity of Srd5a1 in steroid metabolism. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Finasteride may interact with Srd5a1 via Srd5a2, contributing to the regulation of steroid hormone metabolism.",
